The production gate change correctly hard-fails malformed count/hash fields and the added tests pass. The only finding is a low-severity weakness in one regression assertion.

Review comment:

- [P3] Match the ok line with an extended regex — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-t1c/scripts/tests/test_check_governed_surface_pin.sh:313-313
  When this guard is supposed to reject any accidental `ok    governed-surface-pin` line, the plain `grep` treats `+` literally, so the pattern only matches `ok +governed-surface-pin` and would miss the actual ok output with spaces. Use `grep -E` here, or a basic-regex-compatible space match, so this regression check exercises the intended no-ok-line contract.
